From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ricardo Pardini <ricardo@pardini.net>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 00:40:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath10k: WCN3990: skip quiet mode and scan channel stats
 (WIP)

The WCN3990 WLAN firmware on MSM8998 (WLAN.HL.1.0.c6) crashes the modem
(wlan_process / DOG_HB) shortly after the interface comes up. Same
workarounds as reported for SDM660/SM8150 WCN3990:
- don't send the pdev quiet mode command (the firmware advertises
  THERM_THROT anyway)
- don't request channel stat events in scans
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/thermal.c | 4 ++++
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/wmi.c     | 4 +++-
 2 files changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/thermal.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/thermal.c
index 9ff7de0abd12..6e1c4b71e5dd 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/thermal.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/thermal.c
@@ -143,6 +143,10 @@ void ath10k_thermal_set_throttling(struct ath10k *ar)
 	if (!ar->wmi.ops->gen_pdev_set_quiet_mode)
 		return;
 
+	/* WCN3990 firmware advertises THERM_THROT but crashes on the quiet mode command */
+	if (QCA_REV_WCN3990(ar))
+		return;
+
 	if (ar->state != ATH10K_STATE_ON)
 		return;
 
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/wmi.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/wmi.c
index e57588c19c80..c470cafcba2d 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/wmi.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/wmi.c
@@ -7095,7 +7095,9 @@ void ath10k_wmi_start_scan_init(struct ath10k *ar,
 		| WMI_SCAN_EVENT_FOREIGN_CHANNEL
 		| WMI_SCAN_EVENT_FOREIGN_CHANNEL_EXIT
 		| WMI_SCAN_EVENT_DEQUEUED;
-	arg->scan_ctrl_flags |= WMI_SCAN_CHAN_STAT_EVENT;
+	/* WCN3990 firmware crashes (wlan_process) when asked for channel stats during scans */
+	if (!QCA_REV_WCN3990(ar))
+		arg->scan_ctrl_flags |= WMI_SCAN_CHAN_STAT_EVENT;
 	arg->n_bssids = 1;
 	arg->bssids[0].bssid = "\xFF\xFF\xFF\xFF\xFF\xFF";
 }
-- 
